  "bridges": [
    {
      "from": "safebox",
      "to": "lovestruck",
      "kind": "explicit-reference",
      "reason": "Safebox opens with “Mutual, that’s the word,” the line from section VI of Lovestruck. There, reciprocity is what a new love has to live up to; in Safebox it becomes the key to intimacy itself, the condition for opening up and keeping each other’s heart safe."
    },
    {
      "from": "lovestruck",
      "to": "fears",
      "kind": "explicit-reference",
      "reason": "Fears names Lovestruck in its opening note: 2025 began “by wishing” with that poem, 2026 begins “by facing” with this one. The New Year’s poem returns, but the gesture turns inward, from manifesting a love still to come to confronting fear as “a constant in my life’s equation.”"
    },
    {
      "from": "i-loved-so-very-deep",
      "to": "photons",
      "kind": "explicit-reference",
      "reason": "Photons retakes the central line of I loved so very deep: “that it almost got me blind” becomes “that it almost made me blind.” What was a remembered devotion becomes a literal image: looking up to the sun for someone’s light, overexposure, burning, and a darkened tale."
    },
    {
      "from": "i-write-poems",
      "to": "a-zombie-camouflaged",
      "kind": "interpretive",
      "reason": "Interpretive reading: I write poems treats writing as shelter, a way “to sometimes stay” and take refuge in oneself. In A zombie camouflaged the notebook becomes a morgue where longings are “destined to stay,” and writing as a coping mechanism “turned into a gun”: the refuge becomes the site of the wound, and of survival."
    },
    {
      "from": "grandmas-in-danger-of-extinction",
      "to": "a-sublime-experience",
      "kind": "shared-image",
      "reason": "Shared image: love that is timeless and “sublime.” In Grandmas it is the grandmother’s love that “transcends space and time” as she dies; months later A sublime experience turns that into a definition of love itself, “ever changing and timeless.”"
    },
    {
      "from": "en-un-universo-paralelo",
      "to": "desde-el-otro-lado",
      "kind": "shared-image",
      "reason": "Shared image: a love lived on another side of reality. En un universo paralelo places the shared life in another universe precisely because in this one it ended; Desde el otro lado wants to cross the limits and live it “desde el otro lado,” where time is cyclical, not linear."
    },
    {
      "from": "a-missing-gear",
      "to": "armored-as-knights",
      "kind": "shared-image",
      "reason": "Shared image: the heart as a stalled machine. A missing gear keeps one person’s machinery from gleaming and asks for “another motor,” not an anchor; Armored as knights widens it to a generation whose fears “lock their gears,” where “nothing moves if nothing changes.”"
    },
    {
      "from": "forgive-myself",
      "to": "bottle-of-wine",
      "kind": "shared-image",
      "reason": "Shared image: wine as what loosens the words. In Forgive myself “a glass of wine, pen and paper” start the verses of a chapter he cannot close; in Bottle of wine the uninhibited night gives way to the morning after, coming back to himself “one thought at a time.”"
    }
  ]
}
